# Valkivid3 (public vTual template)

Self-contained Tailwind v4 tree (`src/valkivid3/{layouts,components,composables,views,assets}`) for `/vtual`, `/vtual/vtubers/:slug`, `/vtual/managements/:slug`. Routes opt in with `meta.template: 'valkivid3'`; `App.vue` sets `body.vk3-page`.

- **FROZEN:** `VkStr1VtualHomeView.vue` and its exclusive components (`VkStr1HeroSlider`, `VkStr1PlatformStats`, `VkStr1VtuberLiveDirectory`, `VkStr1ContentFeed`, `VkStr1SectionEvents`, `VkStr1SectionCountdown`, `VkStr1ChannelBanner`) are production-ready and must not be edited without explicit user permission, then diffed against the visual baseline in `src/valkivid3/.baseline/`.
- **CSS is imported only by `VkStr1Layout.vue`** (lazy chunk). No Tailwind preflight (a global reset would destroy Bootstrap); utilities nest under `.vk3-root` as **descendant** selectors, so utilities placed on `.vk3-root` itself never match — root background/text/min-height live in `@layer base`, presentation utilities go on children.
- Never use `@import … important(.vk3-root)` — Tailwind 4.3 emits a fake `@media important(...)` that Vite/lightningcss rejects.
- **Bootstrap ships unlayered `!important` utilities** that load after this chunk, so layered Tailwind (`dark:bg-*`) loses to them. The unlayered wrappers in `valkivid3.css` (`.vk3-root .bg-primary`, `.vk3-root .hover:bg-accent-500:hover`, `.vk3-root .dark\:text-gray-900`, …) are load-bearing — do not delete them as "duplicates".
- **Theme forks per mode** in `@layer base`: primary/accent `#475569` light / `#94a3b8` dark; `dark:` is a class variant driven by `html.dark` + `str1-color-theme` (default dark when storage is empty; leaving `/vtual` removes `html.dark`; AdminLTE keeps `data-bs-theme`). Never collapse a fork to one value — the light fork holds WCAG ≥ 7:1 on white.
- **Buttons:** fills fork opposite to labels (`bg-accent`/`bg-primary` CTAs use `text-white dark:text-gray-900`); `bg-primary` hovers via `hover:bg-primary-500`, `bg-accent` via its own `hover:bg-accent-500` (never reuse `primary-500` on accent — dark values collide). Any element with a hover fill forks its label too.
- **Error panel pattern:** async failures render a retryable panel (key `<scope>.retry`), not bare `text-danger` text.
- **Presentation decisions are pure functions** in `src/utils/vtualPresentation.ts` (`channelSyncedTime`, `regionNotice`) and `src/utils/vtualJsonLd.ts`, so they are testable without a DOM. Never render a placeholder timestamp; never hide a region-restricted card (show the notice).
- **SWR key rule:** the guest profile cache key includes the filter tuple (`platform`/`type`/`sort`). Any new query param on `vtual/public/vtubers/{slug}` must be added to that key in the same change, or a filtered request poisons the unfiltered slot.
- **LIVE badge** comes from the backend predicate (`LiveContentScope::applyIsLiveSelect()`); never re-derive it client-side.
- Content filters mirror into the URL via `useVtualProfileQuery` (`?platform=&type=&sort=&page=`, normalized `router.replace`, `sort=newest`/`page=1` omitted) and seed from `route.query` on mount.

Details: [docs/ui-patterns.md](../../docs/ui-patterns.md), [docs/head-meta.md](../../docs/head-meta.md).
